              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Jammed or Malfunctioning Lock</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Sometimes the lockout is not caused by a missing key â€” the key is right in your hand but the lock will not turn. A jammed, sticky, or worn deadbolt can be just as much of a lockout as a lost key, and forcing a jammed lock risks snapping the key or damaging the cylinder further.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Our technicians diagnose the source of the jam on-site. Common causes include a misaligned strike plate, a worn cylinder, loose internal components, a bent bolt, or accumulated debris inside the cylinder. Many of these issues are repairable on the same visit without full lock replacement.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            If the lock has reached the end of its service life or cannot be reliably repaired, we carry replacement hardware and can install a new <a href="/services/deadbolt-installation/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">deadbolt</a> or <a href="/services/lock-change/" class="text-[#A61E22] hover:underline font-medium">complete lock set</a> immediately, keyed to your choice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Card 5 -->
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-8 border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-lg transition">
          <div class="w-14 h-14 bg-[#A61E22]/10 rounded-2xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-7 h-7 text-[#A61E22]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 12l8.954-8.955c.44-.439 1.152-.439 1.591 0L21.75 12M4.5 9.75v10.125c0 .621.504 1.125 1.125 1.125H9.75v-4.875c0-.621.504-1.125 1.125-1.125h2.25c.621 0 1.125.504 1.125 1.125V21h4.125c.621 0 1.125-.504 1.125-1.125V9.75M8.25 21h8.25" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">New Homeowner & Tenant Lockout</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            Moving into a new home or apartment is a chaotic time, and lockouts are common â€” keys get mixed up, borrowed, or lost in the shuffle. We assist new homeowners and tenants throughout Delaware with both emergency entry and the security steps that should follow any move.
